===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|grc|τετράεδρον||triangle-based pyramid}}, from {{m|grc|τετράεδρος}}, from {{m|grc|τετράς||four}} + {{m|grc|ἕδρα||seat}}. {{surf|en|tetra-|-hedron}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|tĕtrəhē'drən}}, {{IPA|en|/tɛtɹəˈhiːdɹən/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-tetrahedron.wav|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Rho9998-tetrahedron.wav|a=UK}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|tetrahedra}}

# {{lb|en|geometry|nocat=1}} A [[polyhedron]] with [[four]] faces; the [[regular]] tetrahedron, the faces of which are equal [[equilateral]] [[triangle]]s, is one of the [[Platonic solid]]s.

